ths)","- Bilateral myringotomy with tympanostomy tube placement (age 18 months)","- Repeat bilateral tympanostomy tube placement (age 36 months)"]},{"sid":59388,"type":"medications","lines":["Home Medications:","- Polyethylene glycol 3350 8.5g (1/2 capful) in 4oz water daily","- Vitamin D3 (cholecalciferol) 400 IU oral daily","- Multivitamin with fluoride 5mL oral daily","- Omeprazole 10mg oral daily"]},{"sid":59389,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":59390,"type":"family_history","lines":["Her mother is 45 years old. Family history is unremarkable for similar symptoms."]},{"sid":59391,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never. Alcohol: Never. Occupation: Preschool student."]},{"sid":59392,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["She is noted to have a flat facial profile, upward-slanting palpebral fissures, and a transverse crease across her right palm.","Otoscopic examination reveals dull, immobile tympanic membranes bilaterally.","Physical examination demonstrates mild hypotonia and short stature.","One of the patient\u2019s eyes is shown both under visible and near-infrared wavelengths below.","The remainder of her neurologic exam is normal."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":12273,"date":"2020-10-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Neurology","attending":"Dr. Priya Patel","cc":"Worsening muscle stiffness and weakness over the past 4 months","order":2,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[5321],"sections":[{"sid":59393,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Worsening muscle stiffness and weakness over the past 4 months"]},{"sid":59394,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient is a 4-year-old female with established myotonic dystrophy type 1, Trisomy 21, and status post repair of secundum atrial septal defect who returns for evaluation of worsening muscle stiffness and weakness.","She has been followed previously in multidisciplinary clinic and otolaryngology for developmental delay and hearing difficulties, and her mother describes frequent episodes of muscle cramping in the arms and legs, especially in the mornings or after exercise.","These episodes last from a few seconds to several minutes and are sometimes painful but improve with gentle massage.","The mother also notes that the child takes longer than other kids to release objects after gripping them, like when playing with blocks or opening door handles.","At school, the teachers report that she speaks slowly and occasionally slurs her words, although her comprehension is intact.","She is generally social and engages with her peers, though she is less physically active and tires more easily during gym class."]},{"sid":59395,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Secundum atrial septal defect (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Down syndrome (diagnosed 2020-04-15)","- Trisomy 21 (Down syndrome)","- Myotonic dystrophy type 1","- Status post repair of secundum atrial septal defect","- Recurrent otitis media","- Mixed conductive and sensorineural hearing loss","- Global developmental delay","- Reactive attachment disorder","- History of neonatal choanal stenosis","- Feeding difficulties in infancy (resolved)","","She was born at term without complications, but had poor feeding during infancy and mild global developmental delays, particularly with gross motor milestones.","Since then, she has received ongoing physical and speech therapy with gradual progress."]},{"sid":59396,"type":"psh","lines":["- Secundum ASD repair with cardiopulmonary bypass (age 8 months)","- Cardiac catheterization with device closure of residual ASD (age 24 months)","- Bilateral myringotomy with tympanostomy tube placement (age 18 months)","- Repeat bilateral tympanostomy tube placement (age 36 months)"]},{"sid":59397,"type":"medications","lines":["Home Medications:","- Polyethylene glycol 3350 8.5g (1/2 capful) in 4oz water daily","- Vitamin D3 (cholecalciferol) 400 IU oral daily","- Multivitamin with fluoride 5mL oral daily","- Omeprazole 10mg oral daily"]},{"sid":59398,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":59399,"type":"family_history","lines":["Her father has similar complaints of muscle stiffness and hand weakness, especially in cold weather or after carrying groceries.","Family history is negative for seizures or intellectual disability."]},{"sid":59400,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never. Alcohol: Never. Occupation: Preschool student."]},{"sid":59401,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On physical exam, the child is alert, cooperative, and answers questions appropriately, though her enunciation is somewhat slowed.","She has mild facial weakness and a flat affect.","There is distal muscle weakness in the hands and feet, and after squeezing the examiner\u2019s fingers, she has difficulty relaxing her grip.","Deep tendon reflexes are preserved.","Gait is cautious but steady.","Babinski sign is absent."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":12274,"date":"2021-07-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Psychiatry","attending":"Dr. James O'Brien","cc":"Behavioral concerns regarding emotional withdrawal and attachment","order":3,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[3756],"sections":[{"sid":59402,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Behavioral concerns regarding emotional withdrawal and attachment"]},{"sid":59403,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient returns for psychiatric follow-up in the context of Trisomy 21, myotonic dystrophy, and prior evaluations for cardiac and hearing concerns.","Foster parents report she is often emotionally withdrawn and does not seek comfort from them when distressed.","They also note she displays episodes of unexplained irritability and fear when approached by other children or adults, even in familiar settings."]},{"sid":59404,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Secundum atrial septal defect (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Down syndrome (diagnosed 2020-04-15)","- Myotonic dystrophy type 1 (diagnosed 2020-10-15)","- Trisomy 21 (Down syndrome)","- Status post repair of secundum atrial septal defect","- Recurrent otitis media","- Mixed conductive and sensorineur